#. Warning on the browser approval page when the app asked for a different account than the one chosen. requestedIdentifier is the email or username the app asked for, name is the chosen account's display name.
#: src/features/auth/flow/HandoffApprovalFlow.tsx
msgid "The {PRODUCT_NAME} app asked to sign in as {requestedIdentifier}, but you chose {name}."
msgstr "„{PRODUCT_NAME}“ programa paprašė prisijungti kaip {requestedIdentifier}, bet pasirinkote {name}."

#. Explains where the code comes from, under the title of the browser page where it is typed. Signing in on another device is the label of a button in the app and must match its translation. PRODUCT_NAME is the app name, such as Fluxer.
#: src/features/auth/flow/HandoffApprovalFlow.tsx
msgid "The {PRODUCT_NAME} app on your other device shows it under Signing in on another device. Only enter a code from a device you control."
msgstr "„{PRODUCT_NAME}“ programa jūsų kitame įrenginyje rodoma skiltyje „Prisijungimas kitu įrenginiu“. Įveskite kodą tik iš įrenginio, kurį kontroliuojate."

#. Shown after the user cancelled the sign-in request in the browser. PRODUCT_NAME is the app name, such as Fluxer.
#: src/features/auth/flow/HandoffApprovalFlow.tsx
msgid "The {PRODUCT_NAME} app was not signed in. You can close this tab."
msgstr "„{PRODUCT_NAME}“ programa nebuvo prisijungta. Galite uždaryti šią skirtuką."

#. Report flow: body of the final screen after a report was sent. {productName} is the name of the app. The second sentence promises the reported person is not told who reported them.
#: src/features/moderation/components/report_flow/ReportFlowCopy.ts
msgid "The {productName} safety team will review your report. We won't reveal that it came from you."
msgstr "„{productName}“ saugos komanda peržiūrės jūsų pranešimą. Mes neatskleisime, kad jį pateikėte jūs."

